      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "We are given that $\\det \\mathbf{M} = -2$. We need to find $\\det (\\mathbf{M}^4).$\n\nRecall that the determinant of a product of matrices is equal to the product of their determinants. Specifically:\n\\[\n\\det (\\mathbf{M}^4) = \\det (\\mathbf{M} \\times \\mathbf{M} \\times \\mathbf{M} \\times \\mathbf{M}) = \\det (\\mathbf{M}) \\times \\det (\\mathbf{M}) \\times \\det (\\mathbf{M}) \\times \\det (\\mathbf{M}).\n\\]\nGiven that $\\det (\\mathbf{M}) = -2$, we can substitute this value into our equation:\n\\[\n\\det (\\mathbf{M}^4) = (-2) \\times (-2) \\times (-2) \\times (-2).\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to compute the product:\n\\[\n(-2) \\times (-2) \\times (-2) \\times (-2) = 16 \\times -2 = 32.\n\\]\n\nThus, the determinant of $\\mathbf{M}^4$ is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{32}.\n\\]",
